# Enabled 2026-07-29. Every warehouse query now runs in its own child process,
# so DUCKDB_QUERY_TIMEOUT_MS can actually SIGKILL a runaway query — in-process it
# only freed the waiting user while the query kept burning CPU and holding its
# concurrency permit. Also contains a DuckDB OOM or native crash to one runner
# instead of the whole API.
#
# Safe to enable since the per-runner budget fix: DUCKDB_MEMORY_LIMIT and
# DUCKDB_THREADS are divided across max(DUCKDB_RUNNER_MAX,
# DUCKDB_MAX_CONCURRENT_QUERIES) slots, so all runners together stay inside what
# one in-process session was allowed. Before that fix each runner claimed 70%.
#
# VALIDATE: look for the one-time log line "Child-process query runner ACTIVE".
# If it is absent and you see "the compiled runner script was not found"
# instead, the runner silently degraded to in-process and this flip did nothing.
# Rollback: set this back to `off` and push.
